[{:db/id 17592186119811 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-b249af0d-2baa-56c1-b03f-659223bf8b34"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186317416 :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(E),$ we need to check if the equation $Ex=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[E\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[E\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & -2 & 5 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 16 & -4 & 10 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 11 & -3 & 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}8 & -2 & 5 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -9 \\\\ 11 & -3 & 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}8{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3}+{x}_{4}=4 \\\\ 0=-9 \\\\ 11{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}-{x}_{4}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get a false statement $0=-9.$ Therefore, the system is inconsistent, and we conclude that $b\\notin \\text{Col}(E).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186120397 :question/problem "Consider the matrix given by $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 8 \\\\ -2 & -11 \\\\ 1 & 6\\end{aligned}].$ Determine the value of $k$ for which the vector $b=[\\begin{aligned}14 \\\\ -15 \\\\ k+5\\end{aligned}]$ belongs to $\\text{Col}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "If $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(A),$ then the equation $Ax=b$ must be consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[A\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 8 & 14 \\\\ -2 & -11 & -15 \\\\ 1 & 6 & k+5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & k+5 \\\\ -2 & -11 & -15 \\\\ 3 & 8 & 14\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & k+5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2k-5 \\\\ 3 & 8 & 14\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & k+5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2k-5 \\\\ 0 & -10 & -3k-1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+10{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & k+5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2k-5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 17k-51\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}=k+5 \\\\ {x}_{2}=2k-5 \\\\ 0=17k-51.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for this system to be consistent, we require $0=17k-51,$ which means that $k=3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186118496 :answer-field/correct 17592186118500 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-b249af0d-2baa-56c1-b03f-659223bf8b34" :question/id #uuid "b249af0d-2baa-56c1-b03f-659223bf8b34" :question/math-academy-id "q-35572" :question/problem "The matrix $A$ and the vector $b$ are given below.\nDetermine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(A).$ \nIn the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}$, where ${x}_{1},{x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3},$ and ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, and ${a}_{3}$ are the respective columns of $A.$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -8 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -4\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(A),$ we need to check if the equation $Ax=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[A\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -8 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -8 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 12 & 6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-6){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & -8 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -12 & -6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}-8{x}_{3}=-2 \\\\ -{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}=2 \\\\ -12{x}_{3}=-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=\\frac{1}{2}.$ Substituting it into the second equation gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{2}+4(\\frac{1}{2}) & =2 \\\\ -{x}_{2}+2 & =2 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, from the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+3(0)-8(\\frac{1}{2}) & =-2 \\\\ {x}_{1}-4 & =-2 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we have a solution, the equation $Ax=b$ is consistent, which implies that $b\\in \\text{Col}(A).$ \n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${a}_{1},$ ${a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}=2\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{1}}+0\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{2}}+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{a}_{3}}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}=2\\cdot 0\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}=0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a69e7526-7c64-51e8-b0ec-23524a78858f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a69e7526-7c64-51e8-b0ec-23524a78858f" :answer-field/id #uuid "a69e7526-7c64-51e8-b0ec-23524a78858f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-791e7d26-9d1f-5803-b774-f6e2358c4273" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ed81c627-15f5-5ac5-9a83-8720033ed743" "answer-dab0c485-45d4-554d-af12-2b22d279fbd1" "answer-791e7d26-9d1f-5803-b774-f6e2358c4273" "answer-a421f5cb-8c63-56cc-847e-0b15d335d55e" "answer-158fd3b6-b42a-5e9e-b83d-ee548a2f6fa5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ed81c627-15f5-5ac5-9a83-8720033ed743" :answer/id #uuid "ed81c627-15f5-5ac5-9a83-8720033ed743" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dab0c485-45d4-554d-af12-2b22d279fbd1" :answer/id #uuid "dab0c485-45d4-554d-af12-2b22d279fbd1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{15}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-791e7d26-9d1f-5803-b774-f6e2358c4273" :answer/id #uuid "791e7d26-9d1f-5803-b774-f6e2358c4273" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a421f5cb-8c63-56cc-847e-0b15d335d55e" :answer/id #uuid "a421f5cb-8c63-56cc-847e-0b15d335d55e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-158fd3b6-b42a-5e9e-b83d-ee548a2f6fa5" :answer/id #uuid "158fd3b6-b42a-5e9e-b83d-ee548a2f6fa5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(A)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186120515 :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(E),$ we need to check if the equation $Ex=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[E\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[E\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 7 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -16 & 28 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 7 & 1 & 2 \\\\ \\text{ }0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}+7{x}_{3}+{x}_{4}=2 \\\\ 0=-1 \\\\ {x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}-{x}_{4}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get a false statement $0=-1.$ Therefore, the system is inconsistent, and we conclude that $b\\notin \\text{Col}(E).$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186247190 :question/worked-solution "If $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(A),$ then the equation $Ax=b$ must be consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[A\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[A\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 1 & -8 \\\\ 0 & -3 & k \\\\ 1 & 1 & 10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -3 & k \\\\ -5 & 1 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -3 & k \\\\ 0 & 6 & 42\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -3 & k \\\\ 0 & 0 & 42+2k\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=10 \\\\ -3{x}_{2}=k \\\\ 0=42+2k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order for this system to be consistent, we require $0=42+2k,$ which means that $k=-21.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "activity-2e13e69f-cc53-5df7-b3bb-fe0183b0f351" :activity/id #uuid "2e13e69f-cc53-5df7-b3bb-fe0183b0f351" :activity/title "The Column Space of a Matrix" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186050656 :activity/course 17592186046659 :activity/steps ["step-fa50bb1e-1a73-5c0f-bd3c-bb3e0f4000d9" "step-d8211cae-1c45-5bea-b330-8b808519d1fe" "step-a4bd27de-27e6-5be6-9522-5db3c45dc351" "step-79efb5b1-7822-50f1-9bbf-67d407d6bfd3" "step-8300882e-730c-5fc3-9879-32bb95590678"] :activity/first-step "step-fa50bb1e-1a73-5c0f-bd3c-bb3e0f4000d9" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-fa50bb1e-1a73-5c0f-bd3c-bb3e0f4000d9" :step/id #uuid "fa50bb1e-1a73-5c0f-bd3c-bb3e0f4000d9" :step/content 17592186317416 :step/next "step-d8211cae-1c45-5bea-b330-8b808519d1fe" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-d8211cae-1c45-5bea-b330-8b808519d1fe" :step/id #uuid "d8211cae-1c45-5bea-b330-8b808519d1fe" :step/content 17592186120397 :step/next "step-a4bd27de-27e6-5be6-9522-5db3c45dc351" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-a4bd27de-27e6-5be6-9522-5db3c45dc351" :step/id #uuid "a4bd27de-27e6-5be6-9522-5db3c45dc351" :step/content "question-b249af0d-2baa-56c1-b03f-659223bf8b34" :step/next "step-79efb5b1-7822-50f1-9bbf-67d407d6bfd3" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-79efb5b1-7822-50f1-9bbf-67d407d6bfd3" :step/id #uuid "79efb5b1-7822-50f1-9bbf-67d407d6bfd3" :step/content 17592186120515 :step/next "step-8300882e-730c-5fc3-9879